{
  "about": "The wardrobe catalogue (D611): every body, piece and look characters on Quaternius's bodies are composed from, per slot, by the game (crates/terra_walker/src/wardrobe.rs) and built by tools/characters/build_bodies.sh (a `wardrobe:<body>` step a body), checked by `node tools/characters/wardrobe.ts`. A new piece or look is a row here and a file, never code (D136). slots: what a look fills, one piece each. regions: the parts of a body, each drawn exactly once. bodies: the body's file (`model`: his skeleton, sockets and the fight's clips sampled on him, no mesh); the folder its pieces' game files go in (`pieces`, each <piece>.gltf with its textures shared in textures/); its head piece, shown unless a shown piece holds the head; a bare piece a slot (D600); its default look. pieces: `body` the body it was made on; `source` the file it comes from under art/ (theirs, untouched, D599), with `cut` the region cut_slots.py cuts from it for a bare piece; `outfit` their outfit it belongs to, whose own pairings a mixed one is judged against; `slot` (none: the head); `item` the item it is the look of (none: bare skin); `layer` 0 skin, 1 worn; `regions` the body's regions it stands for, so hides; `colourways` their shipped colours it comes in; `dye_mask` its dye regions (later: the paint job); `tags`. looks: a piece a slot, a colourway, hair (none yet: their hairstyles are not vendored). pairings: every two worn pieces of a body's different slots, written by `node tools/characters/pairings.ts` from their measure through the clips, never by hand: `apart`, `theirs` (one outfit as made), `pass` or `refused` (pokes or opens where neither outfit's own pairing does, or pokes more at rest), with `over` the outer piece, `clips` the clips past 5 mm or opening the edge, `worse` those worse than theirs, `rest` the vertices poking at rest, `poke_mm` and `worst` its deepest; the game composes no refused pairing and no look may wear one. populations are for a later job (by role).",
